      "source": "To access an instance of this type, use the SwiftUI [`Environment`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/SwiftUI/Environment) property wrapper and specify [`authorizationController`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/SwiftUI/EnvironmentValues/authorizationController) as the environment value, as the following example shows:",
      "normalizedSource": "To access an instance of this type, use the SwiftUI [`Environment`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/SwiftUI/Environment) property wrapper and specify [`authorizationController`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/SwiftUI/EnvironmentValues/authorizationController) as the environment value, as the following example shows:",
      "sourceHash": "3763bde2ed65755202988b501fdd286dc3398f9f2083b1ffd56438f096b8baa8",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Overview",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nstruct AuthorizationControllerExample: View {\n    // Get an instance of AuthorizationController using SwiftUI's @Environment \n    // property wrapper.\n    @Environment(\\.authorizationController) private var authorizationController\n\n    var body: some View {\n        Button(\"Sign In\") {\n            Task {\n                do {\n                    // Create the authorization request.\n                    async let request = makeAuthorizationRequest()\n                    // Perform the request and await its result.\n                    let result = try await authorizationController\n                        .performRequest(request)\n                    switch result {\n                        // Process the request's result.\n                    }\n                } catch {\n                    // Respond to any authorization errors.\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```",
